Reason: GameMaker stops a step as soon as it asks for another room and switches rooms before drawing, so the room
being left is never drawn again. Butterscotch drew it once more and only skipped showing that frame. The extra draw
still painted the view surfaces, and AM2R's item screen shows the frozen game straight from the widescreen view's
surface, so the picture it froze was that hidden frame: the item already gone and Samus not drawn.
Upstream: Bug on every platform.

